## 2. Global Conventions (apply to every step)

- **Build check**: every step ends with `lake build` green (warnings about
  pre-existing issues elsewhere are acceptable; new errors are not).
- **Lint**: run `./scripts/check-lint.sh` before considering a step done.
- **Registration**: every new spec file is added to `Spqr.lean` in
  alphabetical import order.
- **No `sorry`, no new axioms**: each step lands fully proven. Abstract
  functions use `opaque` + `Inhabited` + a `takeD`-style total wrapper so
  length lemmas are *provable*, never assumed. Verify with
  `grep -rn sorry Spqr/Specs Spqr/Code/FunsExternal.lean` and
  `scripts/Audit.lean` where applicable.
- **Attributes**: external-model spec theorems keep `@[simp, step_simps]`;
  function specs get `@[step]`, matching the existing house style.
- **File style**: follow `doc/STYLE_GUIDE.md` — copyright header, module
  docstring with Rust source quote, `natural language description` /
  `natural language specs` comment blocks, `**Source**` line.
- **Regression discipline**: any step that *changes* an existing model or
  spec (Steps 1.2, 1.3, 1.4, 4.1) must first
  `grep -rn <name> Spqr/` for all consumers and fix them in the same step.

