Key-derivation predicate (supersedes `jointly_derived`, which is retained as
a corollary-level notion via `derived_from_jointly_derived`):

```lean
def derived_from (rk mk : alloc.vec.Vec Std.U8)
    (rk_old k : List Std.U8) (ep : Std.U64) : Prop :=
  rk.val = update_root_key rk_old k ep ∧
  mk.val = update_mac_key  rk_old k ep

inductive auth_reachable : alloc.vec.Vec Std.U8 → alloc.vec.Vec Std.U8 → Prop
  | step (rk mk) (rk_old k : List Std.U8) (ep : Std.U64)
      (h : derived_from rk mk rk_old k ep) : auth_reachable rk mk
```

