## 6. Risk Register & Resolved Design Decisions

| # | Risk / decision | Resolution in this plan |
|---|-----------------|-------------------------|
| R1 | `black_box` axiom blocks `compare_spec` (new finding) | Step 1.5 models it as identity — semantically correct (it is an optimisation barrier, not a semantic operation) |
| R2 | Flatten model of `concat` cannot be unconditionally `ok` (`Usize.max` overflow) | overflow-guarded model + length preconditions threaded through `update_spec`/`mac_*_spec` (Step 1.6); documented in each docstring |
| R3 | Changing hmac/hkdf models may break non-authenticator specs (chain, v1 send paths call them) | mandatory consumer grep + full `lake build` in Steps 1.2–1.4; fix-ups land in the same step |
| R4 | `compare` loop indexes `rhs` at `lhs` indices (asymmetric panic) | `compare_spec` precondition decided during the Step 3.1 proof (equal length suffices at both call sites) |
| R5 | Existing `jointly_derived` consumers (`IntoPb`, `FromPb`) must not break | `jointly_derived` retained; `derived_from_jointly_derived` bridge proved in Step 2.1 *before* `update_spec` is restated in Step 4.1 |
| R6 | Structure eta for `from_pb_into_pb_id` | Lean 4 structures have definitional eta; fall back to field-wise statement if the extraction interferes |
| R7 | Crypto-level claims about uninterpreted functions | stated only as conditional theorems with named `Prop` premises (D17/D18); axiom count is *reduced*, never increased |
| R8 | `aeneas-config.yml` / Rust sources | **no changes required** — all enrichment is in the Lean model/spec layer; `src-modifications.diff` untouched |

*(Optional, longer term, out of scope for the checklist)*: instantiate
`hkdf_bytes` concretely from `hmac_bytes` per RFC 5869
(`PRK = HMAC(0³², ikm)`, `T(1) = HMAC(PRK, info ++ 0x01) = root_key`,
`T(2) = HMAC(PRK, T(1) ++ info ++ 0x02) = mac_key`), parameterised by the
algorithm with block alignment expressed via `hash_len` — making
`update_root_key_eq_T1`/`update_mac_key_eq_T2` theorems. Until then these
remain documented design facts.

